        "Text":  "5. Conclusions",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
        "W":  0,
        "H":  0
    },
    {
        "Text":  "Personal Extreme Programming (PXP) is a software",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
        "W":  0,
        "H":  0
    },
    {
        "Text":  "development process for a single person team. It is based on the",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
        "W":  0,
        "H":  0
    },
    {
        "Text":  "values of Extreme Programming (XP) i.e. simplicity,",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
        "W":  0,
        "H":  0
    },
    {
        "Text":  "communication, feedback, and courage. It works by keeping the",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
        "W":  0,
        "H":  0
    },
    {
        "Text":  "important aspects of XP and refining the values so that they can",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
        "W":  0,
        "H":  0
    },
    {
        "Text":  "fit in a lone programmer situation.",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
        "W":  0,
        "H":  0
    },
    {
        "Text":  "PXP can still be refined and improved. It is in the tradition of",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
        "W":  0,
        "H":  0
    },
    {
        "Text":  "XP practitioners to vary XP to encompass whatever works. We",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
        "W":  0,
        "H":  0
    },
    {
        "Text":  "hope that PXP inherits these pragmatic roots, as well. Giving up",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
        "W":  0,
        "H":  0
    },
    {
        "Text":  "XP tenets like pair programming is not necessarily a tragedy.",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
        "W":  0,
        "H":  0
    },
    {
        "Text":  "We still believe that following XP strictly is a more effective",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
        "W":  0,
        "H":  0
    },
    {
        "Text":  "way to pursue multi-person projects. But we are also convinced",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
        "W":  0,
        "H":  0
    },
    {
        "Text":  "that many of the XP practices and methods can be applied to",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
        "W":  0,
        "H":  0
    },
    {
        "Text":  "individual work.",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
        "W":  0,
        "H":  0
    },
    {
        "Text":  "The PXP approach tries to balance between the \"too heavy\" and",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
        "W":  0,
        "H":  0
    },
    {
        "Text":  "the \"too light\" methodologies. PXP will inject the right amount",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
        "W":  0,
        "H":  0
    },
    {
        "Text":  "of rigor for the situation without overburdening the team with",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
        "W":  0,
        "H":  0
    },
    {
        "Text":  "unnecessary bureaucracy.",
        "X":  0,
        "Y":  0,
